# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and MUST NOT be committed.
#
# These VITE_* values are compiled into the browser bundle by design and are
# therefore PUBLIC. That is safe ONLY because Row Level Security on every table
# is sound. See supabase/migrations/20260806000000_lock_down_app_settings.sql —
# a permissive RLS policy turns the publishable key into a credential.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THIRD-PARTY CREDENTIALS DO NOT BELONG HERE AND DO NOT BELONG IN app_settings.
#
# A VITE_* variable is compiled into the bundle, so putting an Airtable PAT or an
# Anthropic key here would expose it exactly as storing it in app_settings did.
# They live in server-side secrets and are reached through a proxy.
#
# Rotation is a secrets change, not a schema change and not a code change.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
